  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nVery stable pattern will persist into the early part of next week.\nExpansive mid level ridge through the middle of the country will\nshift east slightly and be aligned from  the lower Mississippi \nValley into the lower Great Lakes through the weekend. This ridge \nwill get suppressed early next week as a short wave lifts across the \nPlains and then moves through the Great Lakes Tuesday into Wednesday.\n\nDry easterly low level flow will continue through the rest of the\nweek. Winds will get more of a southerly component as the surface\nhigh along the Atlantic seaboard retrogrades into the central\nAppalachians. It looks like a weak front may drop south across the\narea Monday night and then wash out by Wednesday. Limited moisture\nmeans it will stay dry.\n\nTemperatures will stay pretty close to persistence for the rest of\nthe week and then warm up a bit next week.",
